Subject: [PATCH 8/8] mnt: fix the double free of private mount data on failure

Found on the tablet, with 0007 in place: the first boot with sdcardfs
crash-looped. The kernel oopsed in __kmalloc, called from SELinux parsing the
options of the sdcardfs mount, on a freelist pointer of 0x00000006000003f7 --
which is mask=6 and gid=1015 (0x3f7), the sdcardfs mount options, written
into an object the allocator thought was free.

The 3.10 port of "mnt: Add filesystem private data to mount points" (part of
0007, from LineageOS kenzo) frees mnt->mnt.data inside free_vfsmnt(), and
also frees it explicitly right before calling free_vfsmnt() in the error
paths of vfs_kern_mount() and clone_mnt(). Every failed mount of a
filesystem with private mount data therefore kfree()s the same pointer
twice. The out-of-memory path does the same with mnt_free_id(), which this
tree's free_vfsmnt() also calls already.

It never showed on kenzo's Android 8, whose sdcard daemon mounted sdcardfs
right the first time. Pie's tries the newer options first (derive_gid,
default_normal), which this sdcardfs does not know: two failed mounts, two
double frees, and the next mount writes its options into a freed object.

The fix is the shape Android's own later kernels have: free_vfsmnt() owns
the cleanup, and the error paths just call it.
---
diff --git fs/namespace.c fs/namespace.c
index b015932..eaab299 100644
--- fs/namespace.c
+++ fs/namespace.c
@@ -789,7 +789,6 @@ vfs_kern_mount(struct file_system_type *type, int flags, const char *name, void
 	if (type->alloc_mnt_data) {
 		mnt->mnt.data = type->alloc_mnt_data();
 		if (!mnt->mnt.data) {
-			mnt_free_id(mnt);
 			free_vfsmnt(mnt);
 			return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 		}
@@ -799,7 +798,6 @@ vfs_kern_mount(struct file_system_type *type, int flags, const char *name, void
 
 	root = mount_fs(type, flags, name, &mnt->mnt, data);
 	if (IS_ERR(root)) {
-		kfree(mnt->mnt.data);
 		free_vfsmnt(mnt);
 		return ERR_CAST(root);
 	}
@@ -897,7 +895,6 @@ static struct mount *clone_mnt(struct mount *old, struct dentry *root,
 	return mnt;
 
  out_free:
-	kfree(mnt->mnt.data);
 	free_vfsmnt(mnt);
 	return ERR_PTR(err);
 }
